Step by step Migration plan

This is a  General Migration Plan and it is designed to be platform-agnostic. It outlines the phased migration of Amazethu's infrastructure to platforms explored, starting with the platform with the highest ranking number and also starting with most resource-intensive service, botai, to ensure stability before moving the be-app and fe-web. The choice of starting with botai first was based on the service with the highest or most demanding compute resources.

Phase 1: botai
Milestone 1: Platform Account Setup
Task 1.1: Create a Team Workspace with our dev account on the platform
Task 1.2: Connect the GitHub Repository to the account
Milestone 2: Resource Provisioning
Task 2.1: Create a Private Service named botai-stag. For initial testing this will be public but once done, it will be set back to Private
Task 2.2: Select the appropriate compute resource for botai
Task 2.3: Set runtime to docker
Task 2.4: Set root directory to backends/botai
Task 2.5: Configure health check endpoint
Milestone 3: Environment Variables and Secrets Setup: The secrets will follow a hybrid approach; 1. Manual Seed (Once): Manually add "Infrastructure Secrets" (e.g., MONGO_URI, DATABASE_PASSWORD) directly into the platform's dashboard. 2. Workflow Managed (Continuous): Use the platform's CLI (like render-cli or railway-cli) within our GitHub Actions to sync "Application Config" during deployments. Overall  in retrieving the values, the vars on GitHub actions can be used whereas for secrets, the secrets manager on AWS can be used
Task 3.1: Add secrets to platform dashboard.
Task 3.2: MongoDB Atlas Network Access Setup. IP Whitelisting, etc.
Task 3.3: Create new secrets on Github Actions such as project ID,etc if need be.
Milestone 4: CI/CD Integration and Deployment
Task 4.1:Create GitHub workflow file, eg: .github/workflows/[platform]-botai-deploy-stag.yml
Task 4.2:Perform the Initial Deployment and monitor logs for successful build
Milestone 5: Networking & Service Discovery
Task 5.1:Generate the Internal Hostname (e.g., http://botai-stag:5000) for private communication with be-app.
Task 5.2:Provision a Temporary Public URL (e.g., botai-stag.onrender.com) to allow external testing with APIdog.
Task 5.3:Create new subdomains on squarespace and map the Custom Sub-domain (e.g., micro[platform-name].learn.stag.amaspeak.app) for our domain name testing.
Task 5.4: Get DNS records (CNAME) from platform
Task 5.5: Update CNAME record in Squarespace DNS
Task 5.6: Verify SSL certificate is issued
Task 5.7: Test service is accessible via custom domain
Milestone 6: Testing & Validation (Health & Monitoring)
Task 6.1: Verify service starts without any errors
Task 6.2: Endpoint Testing - test the endpoints using apidog while monitoring logs, etc
Task 6.3: Monitor and assess spin up time if any

Phase 2: be-app
Milestone 1: Resource Provisioning
Task 1.1: Create a Web Service named be-app-stag
Task 1.2: Select the appropriate compute resource for be-app
Task 1.3: Set runtime to docker
Task 1.4: Set root directory to backends/be-app
Task 1.5: Configure health check endpoint
Milestone 2: Environment Variables and Secrets Setup: same as was done for botai
Task 2.1: Add secrets to platform dashboard. CRITICAL: Update BOT_API_URL to point to new platform's botai internal URL. eg:BOT_API_URL=http://botai-stag:5000
Task 2.2: IP Whitelisting in MongoDB Atlas
Task 2.3: Create new secrets on Github Actions such as project ID,etc if need be.
Milestone 3: CI/CD Integration and Deployment
Task 3.1: Create GitHub workflow file: .github/workflows/[platform]-be-app-deploy-stag.yml
Task 3.2: Perform initial deployment and monitor logs for successful build
Milestone 4: Networking & Service Discovery
Task 4.1:  Verify BOT_API_URL correctly resolves to botai-stag internal hostname
Task 4.2: Provision a Temporary Public URL (e.g., be-app-stag.onrender.com) for testing
Task 4.3: Create custom subdomain on Squarespace (e.g., api[platform].learn.stag.amaspeak.app) for our domain name testing
Task 4.4: Update references where necessary, eg: stripe webhook, etc so successful testing can be done.
Task 4.5: Get DNS records (CNAME) from platform
Task 4.6: Update CNAME record in Squarespace DNS
Task 4.7: Verify SSL certificate is issued
Task 4.8: Test service is accessible via custom domain
Milestone 5: Testing & Validation (Health & Monitoring)
Task 5.1: Verify service starts without errors
Task 5.2:  Endpoint Testing - test the endpoints using apidog while monitoring logs, etc
Task 5.3: Monitor and assess spin up time if any

Phase 3: fe-web
Milestone 1: Resource Provisioning
Task 1.1: Create a Static Site or Web Service named fe-web-stag
Task 1.2: Set root directory to frontends/fe-web
Milestone 2:  Environment Variables and Secrets Setup: same as was done for botai
Task 2.1: Add secrets to platform dashboard.
Task 2.2: Create new secrets on Github Actions such as project ID,etc if need be.
Milestone 3: CI/CD Integration and Deployment
Task 3.1: Create GitHub workflow file: .github/workflows/[platform]-fe-web-deploy-stag.yml
Task 3.2: Perform initial deployment and monitor logs for successful build
Milestone 4: Networking & Domain Setup
Task 4.1: Add custom domain in platform (e.g., learn[platform].stag.amaspeak.app)
Task 4.2: Get DNS records (CNAME) from platform
Task 4.3: Update CNAME record in Squarespace DNS
Task 4.4: Verify SSL certificate is issued
Task 4.5: Test site loads via custom domain
Task 4.6: Add the new staging domain (e.g., learn[platform].stag.amaspeak.app) to the Authorized Domains list in the Firebase Console.
Milestone 5: Health & Monitoring
Task 5.1: Verify site builds successfully
Task 5.2: Verify site loads in browser
Task 5.3: Test frontend → be-app API calls
Task 5.4: Test authentication flow
Task 5.5: Test Stripe checkout flow
Task 5.6: Test audio recording and transcription (end-to-end)
Task 5.7: Test on mobile devices
Task 5.8: Verify analytics tracking (Clarity,etc)

Phase 4: end to end testing
Milestone 1: Full Stack Integration Testing
Task 1.1: Test user registration flow (fe-web → be-app → MongoDB)
Task 1.2: Test login flow
Task 1.3: Test audio → transcription flow (fe-web → be-app → botai)
Task 1.4: Test Stripe payment flow
Task 1.5: Test subscription activation
Task 1.6: Test user dashboard and settings
Task 1.7: Test logout flow, etc

Phase 5: Notifications & Alerting
Milestone 1: Configure Alert Notifications
Task 1.1: Configure platform alert notifications (email/gchat)
Task 1.2: Test service down alerts
Task 1.3: Test error rate alerts
Task 1.4: Verify Google Chat alert webhook still works

Phase 6: Update to test domain names and Prod migrations
